Give Docker or Podman the credential for the tenant's container registry

A Docker credential helper for the tenant registry,
registry.<tenant>.antithesis.com. Docker and Podman start the helper themselves,
through the docker-credential-snouty binary that is installed next to snouty. To
use it, add the registry to "credHelpers" in ~/.docker/config.json for Docker,
or in ~/.config/containers/auth.json for Podman:

  {
    "credHelpers": {
      "registry.<tenant>.antithesis.com": "snouty"
    }
  }

Then `docker push`, `docker pull`, `podman push` and `podman pull` sign in with
your snouty credential, and `docker login` or `podman login` is not necessary.
Podman also reads ${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR}/containers/auth.json and
~/.docker/config.json. On macOS, put the entry in the file on your Mac, not in
the podman machine.

get reads a server URL from stdin, and prints the credential for it as JSON.
list prints a JSON object that maps the tenant registry of each profile to its
username. It lists a profile when its repository is on
registry.<tenant>.antithesis.com for its tenant. It does not examine the
credential of the profile. Snouty owns the credential, so store and erase read
stdin, change nothing, and succeed: `docker login`, `docker logout`,
`podman login` and `podman logout` do not fail. Run `snouty login` to change the
credential.

The username is snouty-token. The password is your API key, or your OAuth access
token from `snouty login`. Each get refreshes the OAuth token, so a long push
has the full lifetime of the token. When the refresh fails, get uses the stored
token until it expires, and writes a warning to stderr.

The engine does not give the helper a profile, so get uses the profile whose
settings agree with the requested host: its repository is on that host, and the
host is registry.<tenant>.antithesis.com for its tenant. The selected profile
(--profile or ANTITHESIS_PROFILE) wins when it agrees. Then the top-level
defaults win. Then one named profile can agree; when more than one does, get
fails, and you set ANTITHESIS_PROFILE to select one. A profile whose settings
are not valid, such as an invalid tenant, is skipped, also when it is the
selected profile. Environment variables, such as ANTITHESIS_TENANT,
ANTITHESIS_REPOSITORY and ANTITHESIS_API_KEY, apply to every profile. The engine
starts the helper in any working directory, such as a cloned repository, so the
helper does not read a ./.snouty.toml. It reads the global settings file, and a
settings file that --settings or SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH names.

When no profile agrees with the host, get prints "credentials not found in
native keychain" and exits with status 1, as Docker and Podman expect. Each
other error goes to stdout as one line, where the engine shows it, and to stderr
in full.

Examples:
  echo registry.acme.antithesis.com | snouty docker-credential get
  snouty docker-credential list

Usage: snouty docker-credential [OPTIONS] <ACTION>

Arguments:
  <ACTION>
          The credential helper action that the engine requests

          Possible values:
          - get:   Print the credential for the server URL on stdin
          - store: Read a credential from stdin and keep nothing
          - erase: Read a server URL from stdin and erase nothing
          - list:  Print the tenant registry of each profile whose repository is
            on it

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
